---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
const url = (path) => `${base}${path}`;
---
<BaseLayout title='About Chris Miles — Miles Physio' description='Meet Chris Miles, Clinical Director at Miles Physio. Discover his background in physiotherapy and biomechanics, and a personal approach to your care.' bodyClass='about-page' styles={['/about.css?v=1']} apos={false}>
<main id="main">
<section class="section about-hero"><div class="about-breadcrumb"><a href={url('/')}>Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span>About Miles Physio</span></div><div class="about-hero-grid"><div class="about-hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow"><span class="mini-line"></span> About Miles Physio</p><h1>Understanding<br>movement starts<br>with understanding<br><em>you.</em></h1><p class="about-lead">What you want to get back to matters.<br>So does how you feel about getting there.</p><p>At Miles Physio, we combine specialist knowledge of how the body moves with time to listen, explain and build a plan together.</p><div class="about-hero-actions"><a class="button" href="https://miles-physio.uk1.cliniko.com/bookings#service">Book your free discovery call <span aria-hidden="true"><svg class="arrow-icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 18 18 6M6 6h12v12"/></svg></span></a><a class="meet-link" href="#meet-chris">Meet Chris <span aria-hidden="true"><svg class="arrow-icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 4v16M5 13l7 7 7-7"/></svg></span></a></div></div><figure class="about-portrait"><img src={url('/assets/chris.jpg')} alt="Chris Miles, Clinical Director at Miles Physio" width="998" height="1500" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption><span>Chris Miles</span><span>Clinical Director</span></figcaption></figure></div></section>
<section id="meet-chris" class="section about-introduction"><div class="section-label reveal"><span>01 / Meet Chris</span><span>Your clinician, your care</span></div><div class="intro-grid"><h2 class="reveal">Expertise in movement.<br><span class="blue">A personal approach<br>to care.</span></h2><div class="copy reveal"><p class="large-copy">Chris is a Chartered Physiotherapist with a background in sports science and a master’s in biomechanics—the study of how the body moves.</p><p>Since qualifying as a physiotherapist in 2009, he has worked across NHS and private healthcare. His experience includes neurology, respiratory care and neurosurgery, before specialising in orthopaedics and musculoskeletal conditions affecting joints, muscles and movement.</p><p>He has a particular interest in helping people with persistent conditions such as osteoarthritis. His approach brings together clinical expertise and practical guidance, helping patients understand their condition and take an active part in managing it.</p></div></div><dl class="qualification-strip reveal"><div><dt>Qualified in 2009</dt><dd>Chartered Physiotherapist</dd></div><div><dt>Master’s in Biomechanics</dt><dd>Specialist knowledge of movement</dd></div><div><dt>NHS &amp; private practice</dt><dd>Experience across healthcare settings</dd></div></dl></section>
<section id="background" class="background-section"><div class="section"><div class="section-label reveal"><span>02 / Chris’s background</span><span>Knowledge put into practice</span></div><div class="background-grid"><div class="background-heading reveal"><h2>A lasting interest<br>in <span class="blue">how we move.</span></h2><a class="text-link" href={url('/aposhealth/')}>Explore Apos treatment <span aria-hidden="true"><svg class="arrow-icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 18 18 6M6 6h12v12"/></svg></span></a></div><div class="background-story"><article class="reveal"><span class="chapter-number">01</span><div><h3>Understanding the body</h3><p>Chris’s interest in movement began with a degree in Sport Science, specialising in biomechanics. Physiotherapy gave him a way to apply that knowledge directly to patient care.</p></div></article><article class="reveal"><span class="chapter-number">02</span><div><h3>Developing that knowledge</h3><p>He went on to complete a master’s in biomechanics, developing his expertise in walking patterns and gait modification. His work has included publishing research in peer-reviewed journals and presenting at national conferences.</p></div></article><article class="reveal"><span class="chapter-number">03</span><div><h3>Sharing experience</h3><p>Alongside clinical practice, Chris has contributed to the development of Apos treatment methods and training for healthcare professionals in the UK and internationally.</p></div></article></div></div><p class="background-closing reveal">That experience informs his work at Miles Physio, where the focus remains on the person in front of him: <span>their symptoms, their questions and their goals.</span></p></div></section>
<section id="our-approach" class="section about-approach"><div class="section-label reveal"><span>03 / Our approach</span><span>Built around what matters</span></div><div class="intro-grid"><h2 class="reveal">Your goals<br>help shape<br><span class="blue">your care.</span></h2><div class="copy reveal"><p class="large-copy">A diagnosis can explain part of what you’re experiencing. It doesn’t tell us everything about how it affects your life.</p><p>We want to understand what has become difficult, what you’ve already tried and what a meaningful improvement would look like for you.</p><p>You’ll be involved in decisions about your treatment, with explanations you can understand and opportunities to ask questions. Together, we’ll develop an approach that takes your needs, preferences and everyday life into account.</p></div></div></section>
<section id="values" class="values-section"><div class="section"><div class="section-label reveal"><span>04 / What matters to us</span><span>The way we work</span></div><h2 class="reveal">Care you can<br><span class="blue">feel part of.</span></h2><div class="values-grid"><article class="value-card reveal"><span class="value-number">01</span><h3>Personal to you</h3><p>Your priorities guide the conversation. We take time to understand your circumstances and shape your care around the things that matter to you.</p></article><article class="value-card reveal"><span class="value-number">02</span><h3>Understanding that<br>builds confidence</h3><p>We explain our thinking and give you practical guidance, helping you feel better equipped to make decisions and manage your condition.</p></article><article class="value-card reveal"><span class="value-number">03</span><h3>Working together</h3><p>Where needed, we coordinate with other healthcare professionals involved in your care, helping you access appropriate support.</p></article><article class="value-card reveal"><span class="value-number">04</span><h3>Respect at every step</h3><p>Your concerns, preferences and choices deserve to be heard. We approach every conversation with dignity, compassion and respect.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section id="purpose" class="section purpose-section"><div class="section-label reveal"><span>05 / Our purpose</span><span>Understanding. Confidence. Support.</span></div><div class="purpose-grid"><h2 class="reveal">Helping you take<br>an active role<br><span class="blue">in your care.</span></h2><div class="copy reveal"><p class="large-copy">Our aim is to help you understand your options and feel more confident about what comes next.</p><p>That means combining treatment with knowledge and practical tools you can use in everyday life, with support shaped around your progress.</p><p>Whether you’re exploring Apos treatment or looking for online physiotherapy, we’ll start by understanding what you need.</p><div class="purpose-links"><a class="text-link" href={url('/aposhealth/')}>Explore Apos treatment <span aria-hidden="true"><svg class="arrow-icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 18 18 6M6 6h12v12"/></svg></span></a><a class="text-link" href={url('/online-physiotherapy/')}>Explore online physiotherapy <span aria-hidden="true"><svg class="arrow-icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 18 18 6M6 6h12v12"/></svg></span></a></div></div></div></section>
<section id="contact" class="contact-section"><div class="contact-inner reveal"><p class="eyebrow">Here when you’re ready</p><h2>Let’s start with<br><span>what matters<br>to you.</span></h2><div class="contact-copy"><p>Tell us what’s been troubling you, what you’re unsure about and what you would like help with.</p><p>A free discovery call is a chance to ask questions and find out whether Miles Physio could be the right fit.</p><a class="button white-button" href="https://miles-physio.uk1.cliniko.com/bookings#service">Book your free discovery call <span aria-hidden="true"><svg class="arrow-icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 18 18 6M6 6h12v12"/></svg></span></a><p class="about-call-note">Ten minutes to talk through your concerns and explore your next step.</p><p class="contact-direct"><a href="tel:+447980700940">07980 700 940</a><br><a href="mailto:info@milesphysio.com">info@milesphysio.com</a></p></div></div><div class="contact-ring" aria-hidden="true"></div></section>
</main>
</BaseLayout>
